(12) As shown in the figure, given two points $A(-\sqrt{5}, 0)$ and $B(\sqrt{5}, 0)$, the incenter of $\triangle ABC$ moves on the line $x=2$.
(1) Find the equation of the locus of point $C$;
(2) Draw two rays from point $M(2,0)$, intersecting the locus found in (1) at points $P$ and $Q$, respectively, and $\overrightarrow{M P} \cdot \overrightarrow{M Q}=0$. Prove that the line $PQ$ must pass through a fixed point.
